248
00:10:14,253 --> 00:10:15,387
Were you were limestone?

249
00:10:15,387 --> 00:10:16,248
Who's limestone?

250
00:10:16,956 --> 00:10:18,088
Nobody.

251
00:10:18,088 --> 00:10:18,889
He's a cat.

252
00:10:18,889 --> 00:10:19,916
We have a cat?

253
00:10:19,916 --> 00:10:21,195
How long have we had a cat?

254
00:10:21,195 --> 00:10:23,380
It's not our cat.
It's your dad's cat.

255
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:25,384
Dad has a cat? Where?
At work.

256
00:10:25,384 --> 00:10:27,237
It's your dad's work cat
that he never told us about.

257
00:10:27,237 --> 00:10:29,716
Hey. How come you get a cat,
and we don't?

258
00:10:29,716 --> 00:10:30,956
Can you bring him home?
Can I feed him?

259
00:10:30,956 --> 00:10:31,636
Can he sleep in my room?

260
00:10:31,636 --> 00:10:32,898
Why does he get to sleep
in your room?

261
00:10:32,898 --> 00:10:33,910
I'm the one with no friends.

262
00:10:33,910 --> 00:10:35,824
Nobody's getting the cat.
The cat is dead.

263
00:10:36,652 --> 00:10:38,280
Our cat died?!

264
00:10:38,842 --> 00:10:40,405
Oh, Mike, what happened?

265
00:10:41,438 --> 00:10:45,584
Well, he was so weak,
he couldn't even eat or drink,

266
00:10:45,584 --> 00:10:47,168
So I was kind of holding him,

267
00:10:47,168 --> 00:10:48,422
Feeding him milk
with an eyedropper,

268
00:10:48,422 --> 00:10:50,785
Felt him sort of shudder,
and I looked in his eyes,

269
00:10:50,785 --> 00:10:54,641
And he let out one last
little meow, and... He was gone.

270
00:10:55,053 --> 00:10:57,789
So wrapped him in my shirt,
took him down to the west berm.

271
00:10:57,789 --> 00:10:58,725
Where he liked
to lay in the sun,

272
00:10:58,725 --> 00:11:02,393
And, uh, dug a hole
and buried him. (Inhales deeply)

273
00:11:02,393 --> 00:11:04,829
So what's this?
Chow mein?

274
00:11:12,167 --> 00:11:13,773
Frankie, I'm fine.

275
00:11:13,773 --> 00:11:17,226
I know, but just so you know,
I'm here.

276
00:11:17,226 --> 00:11:19,053
(Mouth full)
yes, I see you here.

277
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,828
And if you need to talk...

278
00:11:20,828 --> 00:11:23,033
Mm. There's nothing
to talk about. I'm fine.

279
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:25,118
Okay, 'cause you seem
a little tense.

280
00:11:25,118 --> 00:11:28,173
I'm tense 'cause I'm trying
to spit, and you're in my way.

281
00:11:28,173 --> 00:11:28,951
You mind?

282
00:11:28,951 --> 00:11:30,536
Okay.
(spits)

283
00:11:31,311 --> 00:11:33,860
'cause if you're sad,
it's okay to be sad.

284
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:37,691
I know that. I'd be sad
if I was sad, but I'm not sad.

285
00:11:37,691 --> 00:11:38,979
Ohh.

286
00:11:38,979 --> 00:11:43,039
<i>So the next few days,
Mike continued to not be sad.</i>

287
00:11:43,039 --> 00:11:44,352
<i>(tv playing indistinctly)</i>

288
00:11:44,352 --> 00:11:45,997
Hey, where's your dad?

289
00:11:45,997 --> 00:11:48,517
I told him the game was on,
but he didn't want to watch.

290
00:11:48,517 --> 00:11:50,386
Then he took two beers
and went into the garage.

291
00:11:50,386 --> 00:11:53,115
<i>(Cheers and applause)</i>

292
00:11:54,138 --> 00:11:55,380
You're watching the game?

293
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:56,807
I'm counting the dribbles.

294
00:12:00,771 --> 00:12:03,842
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!
I just vacuumed! Phone books!

295
00:12:03,842 --> 00:12:08,163
(Sighs)

296
00:12:10,996 --> 00:12:12,920
You're not watching
the purdue game?

297
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:14,521
I'm building a shelf.

298
00:12:14,521 --> 00:12:17,327
(Tape clicks) (sighs)

299
00:12:17,806 --> 00:12:21,701
You're sad. Why can't you
just admit that you're sad?

300
00:12:21,701 --> 00:12:22,771
It's annoying.

301
00:12:22,771 --> 00:12:24,062
Well, I think it's annoying.

302
00:12:24,062 --> 00:12:25,714
That you're bugging me
when I'm building a shelf.

303
00:12:26,355 --> 00:12:28,204
I'm not trying to be annoying.

304
00:12:28,204 --> 00:12:31,674
It's just that I sense
that you're holding things in,

305
00:12:31,674 --> 00:12:34,472
And if you wanted to talk
about it, I want to, you know...

306
00:12:34,472 --> 00:12:36,487
Help you process this.

307
00:12:36,487 --> 00:12:38,804
Frankie, it was just a cat.

308
00:12:38,804 --> 00:12:40,222
Named limestone.

309
00:12:40,222 --> 00:12:42,300
And he died.
In your arms.

310
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:43,277
Nothing to process.

311
00:12:43,277 --> 00:12:47,389
Except profound feelings
of loss, grief, and pain.

312
00:12:47,389 --> 00:12:50,929
Mike, just let it out. It never
needs to leave this garage.

313
00:12:50,929 --> 00:12:53,034
Well, I need to
leave this garage.

314
00:12:53,034 --> 00:12:54,152
Gotta get my hair cut.

315
00:12:54,152 --> 00:12:57,778
Well, I would like to give you
a hug. Can I give you a hug?

316
00:12:59,583 --> 00:13:01,029
Oh.

317
00:13:02,377 --> 00:13:06,011
Okay. Are we good?
Can I go get my hair cut now?

318
00:13:06,011 --> 00:13:09,176
(Sighs)

319
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:13,102
(Axl) phone books!

320
00:13:18,177 --> 00:13:19,272
Okay. Axl.

321
00:13:19,272 --> 00:13:22,065
<i>Now I'm not saying you have to
tell me anything, but...</i>

322
00:13:22,065 --> 00:13:25,295
If a bunch of people happened
to be coming over today,

323
00:13:25,295 --> 00:13:26,650
How would I want to dress?

324
00:13:26,650 --> 00:13:29,344
Would it be more casual
or dressy?

325
00:13:29,344 --> 00:13:32,361
Is there a theme?
Is it "Hollywood"?

326
00:13:32,361 --> 00:13:34,947
Well...
I can't tell you much,

327
00:13:34,947 --> 00:13:36,497
But you're gonna want
to go wait in the basement.

328
00:13:36,497 --> 00:13:38,231
Wait. Right now?

329
00:13:38,231 --> 00:13:39,108
Damn it, sue!

330
00:13:40,035 --> 00:13:41,887
I wasn't supposed
to say anything.

331
00:13:41,887 --> 00:13:43,397
Now go in there
so I don't get in trouble.

332
00:13:43,397 --> 00:13:44,552
What am I supposed to do?

333
00:13:45,273 --> 00:13:48,738
It's not ready yet.
(singsongy) just wait.

334
00:13:48,738 --> 00:13:49,755
(Sue) okay.

335
00:13:51,316 --> 00:13:53,638
<i>This is so exciting!</i>

336
00:13:54,696 --> 00:13:56,048
(Frankie) what's wrong?

337
00:13:56,048 --> 00:13:58,223
My barber's moving
to a damn salon.

338
00:13:58,941 --> 00:14:01,505
Okay. So follow him
to another salon.

339
00:14:01,505 --> 00:14:02,985
I'm not gonna do that, Frankie.

340
00:14:02,985 --> 00:14:05,391
I'm not gonna get my hair cut
at a place called "the gossip."

341
00:14:05,391 --> 00:14:07,339
I just... j...

342
00:14:08,505 --> 00:14:12,093
The cat, my barber...
everything I care about, gone.

343
00:14:12,533 --> 00:14:15,179
Your cat and your barber
are everything you care about?

344
00:14:15,179 --> 00:14:18,387
And the colts. That's it.
I'm done loving things.

345
00:14:21,339 --> 00:14:22,980
(Sighs)

346
00:14:23,916 --> 00:14:26,085
<i>Turns out the other mothers
weren't that psyched.</i>

347
00:14:26,085 --> 00:14:28,129
<i>To help a bunch
of socially disorganized kids.</i>

348
00:14:28,129 --> 00:14:29,316
<i>Hold a car wash,</i>

349
00:14:29,674 --> 00:14:31,030
<i>But they were only too happy.</i>

350
00:14:31,030 --> 00:14:33,135
<i>To dump 'em all on me
for four hours.</i>

351
00:14:33,135 --> 00:14:35,029
Uh, sorry about that.

352
00:14:35,029 --> 00:14:36,674
They're still getting
the hang of this.

353
00:14:36,674 --> 00:14:39,664
Here's your $5 back.
And take a bundt cake.

354
00:14:41,783 --> 00:14:43,016
<i>(Man) Frankie...</i>

355
00:14:43,637 --> 00:14:45,512
<i>Your daughter's
in the basement.</i>

356
00:14:45,512 --> 00:14:47,349
<i>She wants to know
if she can come out.</i>

357
00:14:48,226 --> 00:14:49,418
(door squeaks)

358
00:14:49,974 --> 00:14:53,908
Ahh...

359
00:14:55,224 --> 00:14:56,731
(squeals)

360
00:14:57,410 --> 00:14:59,637
Ahh...

361
00:15:04,062 --> 00:15:07,512
Aah!

362
00:15:09,721 --> 00:15:10,705
Hmm.

363
00:15:12,053 --> 00:15:14,006
(Sighs) sorry about that.

364
00:15:14,006 --> 00:15:15,990
Your car will be in the shop
two hours, tops.

365
00:15:17,113 --> 00:15:18,761
(Sighs)

366
00:15:21,501 --> 00:15:24,060
Roses are red.
Everything else should be.

367
00:15:24,672 --> 00:15:28,037
I only eat red food. Do you want
a tomato slice from my lunch?

368
00:15:28,037 --> 00:15:28,822
No.

369
00:15:30,041 --> 00:15:33,369
(Purrs)

370
00:15:33,661 --> 00:15:36,241
Hey. They sewed your socks
to your underwear.

371
00:15:36,241 --> 00:15:38,817
That's smart. That way,
you'll never lose them.

372
00:15:38,817 --> 00:15:39,853
I guess.

373
00:15:42,477 --> 00:15:43,882
I can reach anything.

374
00:15:43,882 --> 00:15:45,585
On the bottom rung
of the vending machine.

375
00:15:45,585 --> 00:15:47,639
Would you like
some certs or a comb?

376
00:15:48,575 --> 00:15:49,730
I wouldn't mind a comb.

377
00:15:50,104 --> 00:15:51,185
Hmm.

378
00:15:52,055 --> 00:15:55,215
Stick with me. I'm sort of
a big fish in a weird pond.

379
00:15:55,790 --> 00:15:57,279
Hey! Where are you going?!

380
00:15:57,279 --> 00:15:59,599
Just keep walking.
Pretend you can't hear him.

381
00:15:59,941 --> 00:16:01,103
He's taking her away!

382
00:16:01,103 --> 00:16:03,026
Hayley, use my sponge!
I want to wash a car with hayley!

383
00:16:03,026 --> 00:16:05,204
She's coming with me!
(whispers) me.

384
00:16:05,204 --> 00:16:07,530
These guys all have problems,
but don't tell 'em I told you!

385
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:09,235
(Boys yell at once)

386
00:16:09,235 --> 00:16:10,631
Ow!

387
00:16:10,631 --> 00:16:12,055
Oh! Bite me! Bite me!

388
00:16:12,055 --> 00:16:14,636
Don't listen to him.
You can bite whoever you want.

389
00:16:15,231 --> 00:16:16,362
Yeah! Bite me!

390
00:16:16,362 --> 00:16:19,580
(All shouting at once)

391
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:23,141
Hey, hey, hey! Stop that!
Social skills!

392
00:16:23,141 --> 00:16:25,307
Remember your social skills!

393
00:16:25,307 --> 00:16:34,699
(Shouting continues)

394
00:16:35,319 --> 00:16:36,930
Nice, brick.

395
00:16:36,930 --> 00:16:38,112
I gave up my whole day.

396
00:16:38,112 --> 00:16:40,156
And organized
that stupid fund-raiser

397
00:16:40,156 --> 00:16:42,137
'cause I thought you wanted
to save social group.

398
00:16:42,137 --> 00:16:43,034
I thought you cared!

399
00:16:43,034 --> 00:16:44,795
Nope, I just like hayley.

400
00:16:46,483 --> 00:16:48,830
Hey, a cute girl
who's a little strange.

401
00:16:48,830 --> 00:16:51,196
Just plops into my lap?
That doesn't happen every day.

402
00:16:51,863 --> 00:16:53,571
The pretty ones usually
have it all together.

403
00:16:53,571 --> 00:16:55,231
(Sighs) great.

404
00:16:55,231 --> 00:16:58,940
I'm wet, my feet are freezing,
I got cake down my shirt...

405
00:16:59,629 --> 00:17:01,874
(sighs) I'm taking a shower
and going to bed.

406
00:17:01,874 --> 00:17:04,309
It's only 7:00.
I don't care!

407
00:17:07,095 --> 00:17:10,429
(Snoring)

408
00:17:10,652 --> 00:17:13,008
Mike. Mike. Wake up.

409
00:17:13,008 --> 00:17:14,419
We forgot sue's birthday.

410
00:17:14,419 --> 00:17:16,142
Huh? What are you
talking about?

411
00:17:16,142 --> 00:17:17,867
The leap year day.
I think it's today.

412
00:17:17,867 --> 00:17:19,650
Like, yesterday today.
We missed it.

413
00:17:19,650 --> 00:17:21,355
How could you forget
her birthday?

414
00:17:21,355 --> 00:17:23,952
It's leap year. We don't
usually have this day, and...

415
00:17:23,952 --> 00:17:25,582
You forgot, too, you know.

416
00:17:29,472 --> 00:17:32,430
Sue. Sue, wake up.

417
00:17:32,430 --> 00:17:36,680
(Singsongy)
hey. Happy Birthday.

418
00:17:37,023 --> 00:17:38,607
Oh, my God.

419
00:17:39,387 --> 00:17:41,143
Oh, what a surprise.

420
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:44,000
Oh, you got me so good.

421
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,555
Yeah, we got you good.

422
00:17:46,555 --> 00:17:49,691
Oh, and I cried myself
to sleep for nothing.

423
00:17:49,691 --> 00:17:51,839
(laughs)
wait. Where's Axl and brick?

424
00:17:51,839 --> 00:17:55,879
Oh. They're the second wave
of the surprise.

425
00:17:55,879 --> 00:17:57,150
Ooh.

426
00:17:57,150 --> 00:17:59,479
Oh, should I open
my presents now?

427
00:17:59,479 --> 00:18:01,653
Um, you bet.

428
00:18:01,653 --> 00:18:04,847
Ohh.

429
00:18:05,591 --> 00:18:07,822
Get up. Get up.
It's your sister's birthday.

430
00:18:07,822 --> 00:18:08,521
What?

431
00:18:08,521 --> 00:18:11,024
Come on.
Just get up and act happy.

432
00:18:11,024 --> 00:18:12,634
(Brick and Axl,
unenthusiastically) surprise.

433
00:18:12,634 --> 00:18:14,436
Ohh.

434
00:18:14,436 --> 00:18:15,672
Presents!

435
00:18:15,672 --> 00:18:16,942
Aah!

436
00:18:19,466 --> 00:18:22,899
(Gasps) oh!
The Bumblebee sweater I wanted!

437
00:18:22,899 --> 00:18:27,604
(Gasps) Matt loves me in yellow!
Aw, thanks, mom.

438
00:18:27,604 --> 00:18:29,657
You are very welcome.

439
00:18:31,621 --> 00:18:35,121
Your old phone. (Gasps)
my new phone! Aah!

440
00:18:35,121 --> 00:18:36,687
(Clears throat)

441
00:18:36,687 --> 00:18:40,001
<i>Hello? Yes, this is sue.</i>

442
00:18:40,001 --> 00:18:43,951
<i>Why, yes, this is
my leap year birthday. (Giggles)</i>

443
00:18:47,006 --> 00:18:49,810
Oh, that's not for you...
Unless you like it.

444
00:18:49,810 --> 00:18:52,492
Why? Is it a clue?
(gasps) oh.

445
00:18:52,492 --> 00:18:55,884
<i>Are you whisking me
away somewhere?</i>

446
00:18:56,789 --> 00:18:57,557
Yes!

447
00:18:57,937 --> 00:18:59,390
To...

448
00:18:59,675 --> 00:19:01,218
The kitchen! For cake!

449
00:19:01,218 --> 00:19:03,983
Yay!
Aah! Yay! (Laughs)

450
00:19:03,983 --> 00:19:05,513
(lowered voice) cake.

451
00:19:05,513 --> 00:19:08,947
(laughs) we got you good.

452
00:19:08,947 --> 00:19:10,014
(Giggles)

453
00:19:10,014 --> 00:19:12,181
(switch clicks)

454
00:19:15,063 --> 00:19:17,395
Hey, sue,
it's carly on the phone.

455
00:19:17,395 --> 00:19:19,992
Aah! Carly!

456
00:19:19,992 --> 00:19:20,795
(Carly, groggily) hello?

457
00:19:20,795 --> 00:19:22,657
How long have you
known about this?

458
00:19:22,657 --> 00:19:23,676
You haven't
said a word all week.

459
00:19:23,676 --> 00:19:24,877
What?

460
00:19:24,877 --> 00:19:26,732
(Dial tone)

461
00:19:26,732 --> 00:19:27,856
Huh.

462
00:19:27,856 --> 00:19:28,559
(Chuckles nervously) (beep)

463
00:19:29,137 --> 00:19:30,831
Here it is. (Chuckles nervously)

464
00:19:30,831 --> 00:19:36,223
(gasps) patchwork cake.
I saw this on "cake boss"! Aah!

465
00:19:36,223 --> 00:19:37,160
(laughs)

466
00:19:37,494 --> 00:19:39,041
♪ happy ♪

467
00:19:39,041 --> 00:19:41,231
(brick, Frankie, Axl, and Mike)
♪ birthday to sue ♪

468
00:19:41,231 --> 00:19:44,346
♪ Happy Birthday to sue ♪

469
00:19:44,346 --> 00:19:48,029
♪ Happy Birthday, dear sue ♪

470
00:19:48,029 --> 00:19:51,201
♪ Happy Birthday to sue ♪.

471
00:19:51,645 --> 00:19:52,799
Don't forget to make a wish.

472
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:57,565
What could I wish for?
I got everything I ever wanted.

473
00:19:57,565 --> 00:19:58,842
(Inhales sharply)

474
00:20:00,852 --> 00:20:02,759
(cheering)

475
00:20:02,759 --> 00:20:03,983
<i>God bless sue.</i>

476
00:20:03,983 --> 00:20:07,006
<i>As I looked at her
blowing out the bathroom candle.</i>

477
00:20:07,006 --> 00:20:08,882
<i>On her patchwork car wash cake,</i>

478
00:20:08,882 --> 00:20:11,611
<i>I felt like sometimes
I didn't deserve her,</i>

479
00:20:11,611 --> 00:20:13,242
<i>But the good thing about having.</i>

480
00:20:13,242 --> 00:20:15,045
<i>Somebody that optimistic
in the family.</i>

481
00:20:15,045 --> 00:20:17,549
<i>Is that her optimism
rubs off on all of us.</i>

482
00:20:17,549 --> 00:20:19,564
Thanks for helping out
tonight, brick.

483
00:20:19,564 --> 00:20:22,304
Hey, how often do you get to
eat cake at 4:00 in the morning?

484
00:20:22,304 --> 00:20:25,084
Mm.
So you like this girl, huh?

485
00:20:25,084 --> 00:20:25,923
<i>Mom.</i>

486
00:20:25,923 --> 00:20:27,608
No, you know, here's the thing.

487
00:20:27,608 --> 00:20:30,567
You liking someone
is actually very social,

488
00:20:30,567 --> 00:20:31,383
So that's a good thing,

489
00:20:31,383 --> 00:20:34,329
And I shouldn't have been
so negative about it. I'm sorry.

490
00:20:35,413 --> 00:20:38,187
I feel like maybe
next week she'll bite me.

491
00:20:38,187 --> 00:20:39,818
Here's hopin'.

492
00:20:41,721 --> 00:20:44,283
<i>Yep. Sue's optimism
even rubbed off on Mike.</i>

493
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:55,684
Hey. You look like
a tough little guy.

494
00:20:57,490 --> 00:20:58,782
Kind of like granite.

495
00:20:59,752 --> 00:21:00,668
Come here, granite.

496
00:21:04,532 --> 00:21:05,992
(Growls)

497
00:21:05,992 --> 00:21:07,879
(chuckles) I get it.

498
00:21:08,472 --> 00:21:11,341
I'm the same way.
